Conduct a water tenure analysis of ${area}. Use the water-tenure-analysis skill and follow its rules
and its report order. The research must be exhaustive and comprehensive, with ${citation_style}
citations.

First establish the area: ${coverage_question} Use that list to bound every later search, and leave
out other basins unless an arrangement crosses into the area.

I want every FAO water tenure type present in the area and a complete description of each
arrangement: who takes water, from where, when, how much, who decides, who pays, who maintains, who
enforces, what happens on breach, how officials treat it, how secure the users feel, the conflicts,
and who is excluded.

Focus on place- and point-based issues: tie every arrangement to a named place or point (spring,
well, intake, weir, dam, canal reach, river reach, lake, village) with its administrative and
hydrological location, and give coordinates only where a source states them.

Divide the report by tenure type: one section for each FAO tenure type, including the types searched
for and not found. Annexes are welcome: coverage of the area, the catalogue, a gazetteer of tenure
points, the questions for legal assessment, and the source register.

Build the catalogue (sources.csv, arrangements.csv, matrix.md) before drafting and check it with
check_catalogue.py. Deliver the report as a Markdown file. Run an orchestrator and subagents as
needed.
